From 65b27eb9128e1e4ea597cafa429dc3ce44567af8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 13:02:01 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(probe): seed the Probe op from a picked face, edge,
 vertex or round wall

A pick on a Probe op now seeds its touch in the same undoable
SetOperationGeometry command: a planar face gives a Face touch against
its outward normal, a straight level top edge an Edge touch on the wall
under it, a vertex an outside Corner from its X and Y walls, and a
closed round rim or welded round wall a Bore or Boss centre from
Circular's circle fit (Bore when the wall's outward normals face the
axis). Picks the probe cannot touch (a downward or tilted face, a bent
or sloped edge, an inside corner, a cone) are refused by name and leave
the op unchanged. The Geometry tab's selection account names the seed
under the pick chip; no project-format change.

New: operation::probe_pick / probe_pick_round (probe_seed,
probe_from_picks, seeded_params, probe_account); tests in
crates/app/tests/probe_pick.rs; decision in
docs/decisions/171-probe-from-pick.md.

Fixes #171

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
